le "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/22056"} "Georges Tainturier"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Jury"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/22751"} "Rodolfo Terlizzi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Jury"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/23812"} "Harold Van Buskirk"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]]] [:tr {:class "hidden_referees", :style "display: none"} [:th {} "Jury"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/899391"} "Clarence, Greve von Rosen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Unlike the other individual events in 1932, épée pools were scored by a point system, with 2 points given for winning a bout, 1 point for a tie or null bout, and 0 for a loss. The pool standings were determined by most points won, followed by fewest touches received. The individual épée competition had the largest field in 1932, with 28 fencers competing."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The last four World Championships had gone to France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/21763"} "Géo Buchard"] " (1927, 1931) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/21772"} "Philippe Cattiau"] " (1929-30), and they appeared to be the favorites, both easily making it to the final. Buchard, Olympic silver medalist in individual foil in 1920-24, came close to defending his World title, winning eight of 11 final pool bouts, but that was equaled by Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/22648"} "Giancarlo Cornaggia-Medici"] ", who had two tied bouts, while Buchard lost his other three, giving the gold medal to the Italian and the silver to Buchard. The bronze went to Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/22593"} "Carlo Agostoni"] ", who had won a gold medal in " [:a {:href "/results/79044"} "team épée at Amsterdam in 1928"] ", as had Cornaggia-Medici. The French and Italians dominated, taking the top six places, with Cattiau coming in sixth. Cornaggia-Medici would return in 1936 to win the " [:a {:href "/results/82339"} "bronze medal at Berlin"] ", while Buchard would repeat as World Champion in 1933."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/22648"} "Giancarlo Cornaggia-Medici"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/21763"} "Géo Buchard"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/22593"} "Carlo Agostoni"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/22725"} "Sav